WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.625
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:00.625 --> 00:00:05.760
I challenge you to find what is
perfectly in season and ripe,

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:12.530
and then just slice it,
taste it, and serve it.

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:17.330
Recipes are a framework,
but the most important thing

00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:21.980
is the ingredient, where you
find it, how you cook it,

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:24.830
and how you will turn it
into a beautiful meal.

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:33.340
I want you to know what food
is really alive and seasonal.

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:36.850
This is the kind of
cooking that nourishes

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:38.230
the body and the soul.

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:47.140
I want to show you how to buy
food in a farmer's market.

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:51.040
Talk directly to the
people who grow your food.

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:55.030
Go to the market before
you decide what to cook.

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:59.710
That will free you from an
overdependence on recipes.

00:00:59.710 --> 00:01:02.933
Because if you start with
really good ingredients,

00:01:02.933 --> 00:01:04.349
you don't have to
do much to them.

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:11.540
This is the philosophy
of food that we

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:16.100
serve at Chez Panisse and
the food that I cook at home.

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:20.990
We're trying to figure out the
best way to serve it and not

00:01:20.990 --> 00:01:25.190
get in the way of the
real taste of that food.

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:29.600
You can never think about
food in the way you may have

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:31.610
thought about it in the past.

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:36.980
It's about how to use every
part of an ingredient very,

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:37.900
very simply.

00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:45.020
That's the beautiful thing
about this delicious revolution.

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:48.620
The closer that we get to
the source of our food,

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:54.770
the better it is for
us and for this planet.

00:01:54.770 --> 00:02:00.170
I'm Alice Waters, and
this is my MasterClass.

